WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.820
In prehistoric times where dinosaur creatures ruled, the adventures of Dino Ricky began.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:28.800
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:29.640
I'm Mike.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.920
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.020
When you think of shmups, they're generally associated with spacecrafts.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.040
So I guess with the adventures of Dino Ricky, Hudson Soft said,

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:50.020
well, what if we just go all the way back to the beginning and make the prequel to every shmup ever with the caveman times?

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.480
Does that sound right? Do you guys think that's what this was going for?

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.200
I guess so.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.280
Yeah, prequel. Prequel. I was waiting for Jar Jar to show up.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.520
Right. You can't prove that Dino Ricky didn't happen in the Gradius universe.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.140
Actually, you're right.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:11.420
I mean, you know, there's those, those, there's, uh, volcanoes that kind of like tell you that, you know, there's probably a dinosaur somewhere.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.520
Um, cause you know, when there are dinosaurs, there's always going to be volcanoes.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.500
So I, I think it follows.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.560
Yeah. This is less like shmup feeling to me.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.720
It has like a commando Ikari warriors vibe going for it as well.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:32.680
Like, yes, it is a shmup, but I guess like when I look at it from this top down perspective with the art style and everything, it was also giving me commando vibes.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:33.860
Did you guys pick up on that as well?

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:43.260
Yeah, it actually gave me commando vibes so much that it, that it's sort of, it's sort of, uh, surprised me and frustrated me when it didn't play like commando.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:50.040
Because it really feels like it, to me, it feels like it should have that, uh, that sort of, um, gameplay.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.640
I think it's really just the fact that you're shooting straight forward, which like suddenly separates it into the shmup world for me.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:09.540
Yeah. When I, when I first booted it up, I'm like, Oh, finally, one of these land-based, uh, shmups or whatever we want to call them running guns, uh, finally did the thing where you're always just shooting in one direction.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:10.660
Don't have to worry about it.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.320
Um, so yeah, I, I felt the same thing.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:21.820
In the adventures of Dino Ricky, uh, players take control of caveman Dino Ricky.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.540
I actually, it, maybe it's just Ricky.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.040
Maybe he's not Dino Ricky, uh, formally.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.580
Like maybe his parents didn't name him that.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:28.860
Anyway, you play as him.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:30.340
It's a vertical shmup.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:37.260
You start off throwing rocks, you upgrade to other projectiles, and you're throwing these things at dinosaurs, giant insects, birds.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:44.840
You get the idea. Uh, also you can jump in this game, which is, uh, a weird thing to say, but you know, you don't do that in shmups necessarily.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.620
You don't think about, uh, the planes.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:51.780
So here we are with, uh, Dino Ricky and not those planes.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:54.660
I mean, yeah. Do you mean like the, the dimensional planes?

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.620
Yes, I meant the dimensional planes.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.200
The great planes.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:07.860
Okay. So I think I did a good job of, of just setting up everything that you need to know about this game, but we do have to talk about the game, even though we're saying it's just a shmup.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.160
What about it?

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:17.040
Uh, in terms of, you know, shmup, uh, tropes, controls, things that we're used to when we talk about these kinds of games, what things stood out for you guys?

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:24.920
Well, the first thing that stood out for me is like, you know, the, the power up tech tree doesn't make any goddamn sense to me.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:36.220
And I know that this is like, you know, it's not very, uh, core to the mechanics of the game, but I just find it strange that you start with rocks and then, you know, you pick up your little power up fist thing.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.840
And then you switch to butterflies, like right off the bat, totally confused.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:48.060
Um, after butterflies, uh, I think you get boomerangs, which a lot, which makes a lot more sense, even though like a lot of things in this game, it's sort of an anachronism.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:55.560
Um, and then after that, you just immediately go to like, you know, sorcery and you're now throwing fireballs.

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:59.320
And, uh, so I just was completely caught off guard at every moment.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:08.260
I guess if they wanted me to be like on my, uh, like waiting, uh, with bated breath to see what the next power up is going to be, they succeeded.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:13.620
Um, that was the final power up, Sean, the final power up.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.940
Yes. There's one more after that.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:17.500
Okay. Hold on though.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:30.300
Because like, I got a lot of power ups in this game and I had the fire many a times and I never once turned into Macho Ricky.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.400
So I guess we could talk about that.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.180
Well, Macho Ricky, just, just so this way everybody's clear.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.720
It's very much like that game.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:44.040
I'm a gone. If you remember, we did that a couple, uh, like dozen episodes ago where you play as like a little kid and in the jungle.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:51.220
And then if you reach your full capacity of power, you basically just become the bigger, like caveman like version of Amagon.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.880
Well, that's, what's happening here with Ricky.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:57.260
He goes from Dino Ricky to Macho Ricky, but I'm pretty sure.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:01.380
And Joe, you can correct me if I'm wrong here, but you need the, uh, Macho Ricky icon.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.520
You have to pick that up.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:05.200
It's like his face on the, on the power.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.140
Never found that.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.400
Never found it once.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.120
Yeah. I think that's true.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:13.960
I actually only became Macho Ricky once and I didn't know how.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.000
So, but I saw some playthroughs I was watching.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.700
It looks like there is something that I pick up that, that requires it.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:35.840
But I just wanted to mention it because you were mentioning all the projectiles and I, you know, I don't know if we're all aware of what the projectile is when you're Macho Ricky, but you become this, you become this giant muscly caveman and you throw a bunch of giant muscly cavemen that look exactly like you.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:36.960
You astral project.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.920
It is the weirdest looking thing.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:49.480
I mean, that power up, you have essentially, uh, ascended in the game and you're now experiencing what the dinosaurs never could.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:58.460
Well, I always forget if it, cause you know, just my history and biology, you know, it's so long ago since I learned this stuff.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:05:59.840
Did the cavemen used to do that?

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:01.280
Oh yeah.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:13.060
Yeah. I mean, basically this is, uh, I think the entire story of the game, um, is a caveman that has discovered DMT and, and, and sort of has to deal with that.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.020
And that's, that's pretty much it.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:16.620
Yeah. None of this is even happening.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:27.160
If I remember correctly, Hudson soft actually found this exact story on like one of those caveman paintings when they were going through ancient caves and they just recreated this story, uh, which is part of history.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:34.260
It's I'm just so happy that finally video games are, are trying to, to create real art.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.680
To go back to the Dino Ricky weapons, right?

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:53.560
Which are probably the most interesting part of, uh, you know, this shmup there's, you start off with just like throwing rocks and then you move up to, um, the ax and the boomerang and eventually like the fire torch and everything like that.

00:06:53.560 --> 00:07:02.940
But what do these power ups actually mean for you in terms of like surviving in this game and being able to take on enemies more?

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:13.940
Like, did you feel like there is a distinct difference from power up to power up or was really just like the animation and how many you were able to fire changing?

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.580
Well, well, Mike, what was the ax?

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.380
The, uh, well, I'm referring to the manual here.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.560
So I think the ax is the butterflies.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:23.020
So, well, okay.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.340
Yeah. Why'd they call it an ax?

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:25.480
It's definitely not an ax.

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:26.700
They're literally butterflies.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:31.180
Um, unless that's just their very strange way of, of rendering butterflies.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:42.780
I thought it was that like caveman-y looking like rock that's like, that's got, that's like bound into an ax or something or, you know, like, so it kind of looks butterfly-ish, but I can see it.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:46.340
Do I, do I just have some weird, like, am I having a stroke while playing this game?

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:51.260
I don't know. I see what you mean by butterflies, but I can also see the like Flintstones ax.

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:52.640
Okay. All right.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.120
I will grant there be, they being axes then.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:08:07.540
But, uh, to answer your question, um, yeah, I think there is a, a clear superiority to each, um, to each weapon as you get it.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:13.940
Um, whether it's fire rate, um, or spread, um, like the fire is, is insane.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:25.360
Like you could just, like the fact that you can hold the button down and, and it kind of acts as its own turbo button, um, is, it means that it's like, it should be the most powerful one.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:34.820
And I think even just the first step from, uh, rock to ax slash butterfly is, um, enough to be useful.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:39.440
Yeah. I think so much of this game kit for me came down to crowd control.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:45.700
Like, like if I, if I had good crowd control, I was having a much better time than when I had no crowd control.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:09:00.460
Because I think there's just so much going on on the screen that at least for, for my play style, I really need to be able to take as much out, um, as quickly as possible or else I just have no chance in avoiding all of these enemies that are just everywhere.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:13.600
So, so yeah, each, I guess I hadn't really thought about it, but I, now that we're, now that we're discussing it, I do think that each power up, they do a good job of evolving it appropriately with each, uh, with each pickup.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:22.800
Yeah. And it's important to remember too, that like this particular game comes down to how well you perform early on.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:41.320
Uh, if you're, if you like really learn this beginning stages of this game and collect like all the possible hearts that they give out to you and, and power yourself up appropriately, um, you have a large enough spread and pretty powerful weapons to take on most things that are, uh, to Joe's point, like involved with crowd control.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:54.960
And they give you some, they're pretty generous with the hearts here, but granted, if you keep taking hits, you're always going to be stuck around like the three to four range, but you can have like, I think at one point I had like eight hearts after I like figured out the layout for the stages and stuff.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.320
You can have a lot of hearts and hearts in this particular game.

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:02.920
What makes them interesting is that's your, um, your health meter here.

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:07.620
So it's not the typical shmup where you take a hit and then you lose your life automatically.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:12.500
And whether you respawn or restart the stage, that's what usually happens in a shmup in this game.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.200
When you take a hit, um, you lose a heart.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:17.900
And I think your power up goes one down, correct?

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:21.140
Yeah. That's really the biggest difference here.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:41.220
And, uh, I think what sets us apart is, is that like you, your, your punishment for getting hit is your speed goes down, your, your power up goes down and, uh, your heart goes down, but it doesn't go back to like one or zero or however you want to think about it.

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:46.260
Like you, all you need to do is rally a little bit and you can get back to where you were.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:55.240
Um, which I, I kind of wished for a lot of our previous shmups, um, just because I'm used to more forgiving games now.

00:10:55.240 --> 00:11:08.960
And yet if you are playing this for the first time, um, and you don't, uh, know to like, you know, be great early on, get everything you possibly can, uh, just to, to, just to have the best advantage possible, which sounds silly.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:22.160
But I, I really want to reinforce that idea that like, as long as you play your cards right at the beginning, it helps your experience throughout the entirety of the game because you basically just have more health, more power ups, like just to go off of and, and can be a little more risky.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:30.140
Whereas if you're playing with very few hearts and no power ups, you're going to have a hard time of like keeping, uh, the chance to get stronger.

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:42.060
So with this game, while all that's happening, if you play this for the very first time, I was surprised by the amount of enemies and, uh, the patterns of these enemies, like right away.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:47.880
Uh, they're, it's not something where they introduce, you know, Oh, these guys come down in single file.

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:53.260
These guys kind of, you know, moving horizontal lines to your vertical, uh, scrolling.

00:11:53.540 --> 00:12:02.920
It's just like, you get pummeled with rocks and birds that just move in like sweeping fashions very, very fast compared to the speed of Dino Ricky.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:10.780
And that was like surprising to me to the point where I actually had to pull myself back a little bit and figure out like, all right, how do I take down these guys?

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:15.240
Cause I can't just like keep fuddling around with, you know, with them just on the screen.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:19.040
Um, yeah, I, that was like the biggest thing that I noticed too.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:25.140
I think probably maybe because I haven't played a shmup in a while, but man, there was nowhere to go.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:33.360
Uh, with, yeah, I think that they did have interesting patterns and unique patterns for each enemy, but they would just throw them all at you at once.

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:39.020
So the patterns meant nothing because, because to the player, it's just a bunch of crap coming at you and like this crazy web.

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:50.300
Um, I think as far as, uh, as far as like avoiding and dodging things, this was one of the hardest, um, shmups that I can remember to, to just not take a hit.

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:55.020
Yeah. You end up having to just like sort of stare at yourself and just spray and pray.

00:12:55.360 --> 00:13:11.520
Um, and like, you know, in your periphery, well, at least for me, uh, in your periphery, just sort of like get in front of, uh, what you can see coming for you and, and then just focus entirely on dancing around the projectiles that you can't destroy.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:25.140
Um, and it was almost, there were almost times where I kind of wanted a return back to, uh, the old way of doing things with commando, uh, just to get rid of the guys that got past me.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:29.800
Uh, because then it just turns into like, oh, I'm getting hit.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.620
Like, there's no way about how I'm like, if I can avoid it, it's just going to happen.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:56.140
And that's why the power up system is so important with the spread feature of like, uh, you know, how far you spray your, your attacks because the fire one, for instance, I know it's the strongest one, but that naturally just shoots out in a, um, like a rapid V like shape where it switches between left and right.

00:13:56.300 --> 00:14:00.940
And you don't necessarily have to move around the screen, but if you move around the screen, it helps even more obviously.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:07.920
But that spray of just like, oh, well this could hit anything and hits everything often really helps with control.

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:13.540
Whereas if you just had like your rock and you're just throwing it around, I mean, I guess that's the point, right?

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:19.420
You're supposed to feel powerless with just the rock as opposed to fire because fire is what made man so strong.

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:24.540
But you know, it's like the, the spray here accounts for more than anything.

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:27.700
And I'll just say that that's a good mechanic in shmups.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:34.020
I think it's important to think about how you, um, how you attack and what your plan of attack is in these shmups.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:42.780
If you want to get better at them, quick shout out to an article I just wrote on nostalgiacast.com a few weeks ago, uh, which gives a bunch of tips on how to be better at shmups.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:47.720
And one of them involves, uh, that very said spray in the adventures of Dino Ricky.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:50.520
Is it a shout out if it's your own work?

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:52.300
That's who I'm shouting out.

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:53.340
I'm shouting out me.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:54.980
Oh, okay. Great job, me.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.440
From the past. Me from the past.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:57.680
Just like Caveman. Yeah, sure.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:15:01.420
It's like a different guy. Like every seven years, all your cells change over or whatever.

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:02.940
That's like a totally different guy. That was seven years ago.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:05.360
It was only like a week that he wrote, that he wrote it.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.900
But I mean, I'll grant him that.

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:12.820
Yeah, it's a shame I said a few weeks because I could have argued that this was written in the Caveman times and you wouldn't be able to prove me wrong.

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:15.680
Well, a few is subjective anyways.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:19.660
Right, right. A few weeks ago in the grand scheme of the universe was Dino Ricky.

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:33.800
Yeah. The most, uh, unique idea for this shmup is also arguably the thing that is most controversial about this game.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:36.100
And that is the ability to jump.

00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:42.060
Uh, we, we briefly discussed this in the overview, but I think for those of you who need a clearer understanding,

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:52.880
the whole game obviously takes place on land and they've included a bunch of pitfalls, um, water, uh, sand traps and stuff like that,

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:55.940
that you would, uh, be required to jump over.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:16:02.620
So they included a jump button as the secondary thing other than your attack so that, uh, you know, for a brief moment in time,

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:05.540
you are in the air before you land back down.

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:12.640
This is a neat idea, but I feel like the way they laid out the levels is where this goes wrong.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:21.480
If you just had some occasional, like, areas where you have to jump over a pitfall or a, um, a sand trap,

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:23.060
that sounds great to me, right?

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:25.200
Like, okay, cool. That's just part of the level.

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:35.860
But when you put in the desert stage, a hundred plus sand traps all next to each other, then it's like, what, what that, no, the jump isn't necessary anymore.

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:41.100
Now you have to use that other power up that gives you fairy wings to stand a chance against this.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:47.880
So before we like use the fairy wings as the crutch on this, let's just talk about pretend that you could only jump.

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:50.280
How does that mechanic work for you guys?

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:51.800
Are you feeling good about it?

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:53.000
Did they make a mistake?

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:57.800
No, because look, the whole game is, is a treadmill.

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:04.920
And the thing about that is, um, so you're going to continue to move forward.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:08.280
You're just going to continue to walk forward regardless of what's ahead of you.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:21.060
Um, but that, that does not really, it's not conducive to how the jumping mechanic works because when you jump, uh, you're trying to get some kind of, uh, precision as to where you land.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:26.200
And I'm not even like, this isn't even touching upon, uh, the precision of the drum itself.

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:28.560
It's just the positioning that follows.

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:37.940
Um, so you'll end up in a situation where you're jumping on a very small platform and then you have to fight the game itself to stay on the platform.

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:41.120
Um, because you're moving with the screen.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:48.360
And then you got situations where the platform you're on is a very jerkily moving platform itself.

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:52.860
So now you're fighting against the scroll of the screen and then this platform.

00:17:53.280 --> 00:18:01.940
Um, because if you do nothing, like as, as, you know, as opposed to a regular platformer where if you do nothing, you just stay on the platform.

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:04.500
If you do nothing, you walk off the edge and die.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:13.640
And this is where the game kind of falls apart for me because the, um, that is the most frustrating part of this game.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:16.440
And it, it becomes a major part of it.

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:21.000
Like, it's not just the thing that you, that you run into, uh, in certain sections.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:25.060
Like there are certain levels where that is everything.

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:32.840
And I, yeah, this is the most poorly implemented platforming section of a game I've ever seen.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:43.380
Um, yeah, I think that, um, personally, I feel like a jump in a shmup like this could be an interesting and unique idea.

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:48.860
I mean, I don't think there's any problem inherently with thinking like, okay, it's a shmup, but you have to jump over gaps.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:56.160
Um, but the thing is, you know, for the, if you're, if you implement a jump into your game and this is just my personal preference.

00:18:56.160 --> 00:19:00.320
And, you know, maybe people might disagree with this, but I feel like the jump shouldn't be absolutely fucking horrible.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.340
And in this game, the jump is horrible.

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:16.040
It is really like, I like, I guess it's really kind of what, uh, what Sean said, where you, in like thinking of like, I'm thinking of like Super Mario Brothers 3.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:18.940
I know that's a side scroller, but there are auto scroller levels.

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:23.240
The level doesn't scroll independently of you.

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:28.640
Like that, that's just like another way of saying what you were getting at before, where you'll walk off the platform.

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:31.100
Like the platform moves and you don't.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:32.560
That's the problem.

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:36.540
Like that's what, like the platform will just slide out from under you while you're standing still.

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:41.340
So like, yeah, if you're, if you're on a platform waiting for the next platform, you have to be walking with the platform.

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:44.100
It's as if you have no interaction with the platform.

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:50.260
And then the jump itself is really hard to gauge if you have momentum.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.260
Like there are, there are a couple of times where it's like, I'm not sure.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:58.980
I'm pretty sure like the momentum of the scrolling of the screen actually pushes me forward a little bit.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:01.560
Or maybe the screen, I guess, just scrolls under me when I jump.

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:06.800
But there are some times where something is so close, I need to make a tiny jump and I just jump without moving at all.

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:08.280
And I land on the next thing.

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:12.520
But there are other times I need like a little bit of a bigger jump and I'll jump, I'll like run forward and jump.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:17.440
And I will fly all the way across, I'll fly like so far forward, way overshoot it.

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:19.160
I have no idea the momentum of it.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:25.720
So I was like excited about the jump at first, but it just, it was, I was fighting it the whole time.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:26.740
It just didn't work.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:36.000
Yeah, basically if you, if you jump without any other directional input, you're basically like, yeah, the screen is moving under you.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:40.860
And that ends up being you moving a little, a little bit forward.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:45.520
But if you jump with any kind of momentum, you kind of slingshot yourself.

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:54.160
And it's, it's really hard not like to, it's, it's really hard to, to gauge whether you're going to do one thing or the other when you're trying to add any kind of position to it.

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:59.440
Um, so between that and like, I feel like we're talking about relativity right now.

00:21:07.180 --> 00:21:09.680
But how does that like equals MC square?

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:15.040
Like it's, it's kind of a pain in the ass just to wrap your head around how platforming works in this game.

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:23.480
Even just thinking about how they, uh, implement it, like how they explain to you that this is something you're going to have to be doing in this game.

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:31.680
In the very first level, there are, uh, there's water that you cannot fall into, but they put, um, you know, lily pads on it.

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:39.160
So this way you jump onto those pads and they give you like one directly centered lily pad immediately on the screens.

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:41.380
This way you're like, oh, that's where I must go.

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:42.540
And they're large to be fair.

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:45.060
Like it's not a small little, a tile or whatever.

00:21:45.060 --> 00:21:49.140
So you go jump on that and you know, you can still screw that up.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:56.560
I think I did my first time, but if you land on it, then they give you another lily pad and then another one and then another one.

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:57.980
And it's just a series.

00:21:57.980 --> 00:22:00.280
It's not even just like jump once.

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:01.740
Okay, cool. Now you've got the concept.

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:04.920
Maybe later we'll reintroduce some more jumping or multi jumping.

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:06.140
It's right away.

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:09.200
It's like now jump again, jump again, jump again.

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:17.620
In fact, they do this kind of, um, execution more than just the one-off jump or pitfall every now and again.

00:22:17.680 --> 00:22:23.980
They do the execution where it's just, here's a thousand jumps in front of you or a thousand situations to jump around.

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:27.260
That it's almost like they were making the game, building out the levels.

00:22:27.480 --> 00:22:30.560
And then later on they were like, you know, we're going to add this jump mechanic.

00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:33.780
So you've got to add pitfalls into the levels.

00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:36.140
So they're like, yeah, I'll just throw a thousand right here.

00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:42.540
Like I'll just, I'll just make this whole section lily pads and I'll just make this whole section wall to wall sand traps.

00:22:42.700 --> 00:22:49.480
It's, it's not necessarily the way I would have thought to even just, uh, use that kind of mechanic.

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:54.160
You know, if you're thinking about in shooters, um, that involve planes, right?

00:22:54.280 --> 00:23:02.840
Sometimes you can do like in 1942 or maybe it was 43, uh, the extra button allowed you to do a loop de loop.

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:05.220
So this way you were like invincible, right?

00:23:05.220 --> 00:23:08.480
You're now longer on the same plane as the, as everybody else.

00:23:08.680 --> 00:23:17.500
The jump doesn't necessarily, um, you know, contradict that feature, but that is like, that's a better use as like an additional dodge, right?

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:26.180
Then as opposed to an additional pitfall on top of all of these enemies coming at you as you're trying to move forward or staying on your platform even, right?

00:23:26.180 --> 00:23:33.480
Sometimes you have nowhere else to go because you, you have to jump from lily pad to lily pad, or you have to watch out for the hundreds of sand traps.

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:36.940
So you can't really move either, but now you also have to take care of all these enemies.

00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:41.220
I don't think there was a careful balance being applied here.

00:23:41.300 --> 00:23:42.620
I'm not saying they didn't play test it.

00:23:42.620 --> 00:23:49.140
They probably appreciated how hard they made, uh, certain sections of this game if you're not accurately prepared for it.

00:23:49.140 --> 00:24:00.180
But it's not necessarily, like, it's not a good thing to throw like a ton of power-ups and hearts all over the screen to then make it okay to be more chaotic.

00:24:01.880 --> 00:24:22.420
Yeah, I mean, I know that we still have, like, bosses to talk about, but this is the best time that I can think to bring this up, is that, like, if I wanted to play designer for a second here, as we often do, I think the only thing that they had to change to make this a less frustrating experience is to just make it so that you literally had to walk with the screen.

00:24:22.420 --> 00:24:35.440
Like, you had to press up, and you had to, like, like, if you, if you let yourself fall to the back, the screen will push you up, but you have to be the one to actually, uh, decide you're going forward.

00:24:35.780 --> 00:24:51.880
Then, you can be a lot more thoughtful with your, uh, platforming, and not just, like, chuck it and pray, uh, because you know that your character will accidentally walk off the screen, or off the platform, nine times out of ten.

00:24:52.360 --> 00:24:56.020
Um, and I think then you have, like, that's fine.

00:24:56.180 --> 00:25:03.980
Like, I don't know how I would, how I would think about this game if that were the case, because one of the things that bothered me so much is no longer a part of it.

00:25:05.020 --> 00:25:14.760
Yeah, you know what, it's just kind of dawning on me right now, is that, like, what you're talking about, I think it's because they're treating it so much like a shmup that they're treating Ricky as if he's a spaceship.

00:25:14.760 --> 00:25:21.180
And the background is space, rather than, uh, than something he's, he's fundamentally attached to in some ways.

00:25:21.280 --> 00:25:28.320
There's no gravity or friction holding him to the ground, it's just, it's just the, it's space moving behind him, as far as we're concerned.

00:25:28.460 --> 00:25:31.000
Yeah, and then the water is just a danger zone.

00:25:32.440 --> 00:25:41.820
And you gotta believe on some level they knew that the jumping was a problem because the fairy wings, which I'm, I'm calling it that I don't remember exactly what it was called in the manual.

00:25:41.820 --> 00:25:52.800
Um, that ability is one that, like, you just jump, and as long as you have those wings on your back, that jump is infinite now, until you let go.

00:25:52.960 --> 00:25:59.140
Now, granted, once you let go, the wings go away, so, you know, there's a good, like, trade-off there, a good risk factor.

00:25:59.420 --> 00:26:10.300
But you can hover above the stage, eliminating all platforms, while also being able to destroy all enemies, theoretically, below you now, uh, as you're in the air.

00:26:10.300 --> 00:26:25.680
So there's very little, you know, um, there's very little incentive to ever think about, like, using the fairy wings for any other portion than these extra extended long jump sequences that they've made, uh, that you know are in each level.

00:26:25.760 --> 00:26:33.540
There's just gonna be a point where you're gonna have to jump a lot, so might as well use your fairy wings there, and not just for, like, a momentary bliss.

00:26:34.400 --> 00:26:55.040
True that. So, uh, of the four worlds, at the end of each of them, there is a boss fight, uh, that you must do, uh, with either a pterodactyl, or a, uh, I think it's a tyrannosaurus rex, and a giant wasp, or, uh, you know, I don't know.

00:26:55.040 --> 00:26:56.260
A fly. Sure.

00:26:56.540 --> 00:27:00.200
I don't know. And a triceratops, and a, uh, cobra.

00:27:00.380 --> 00:27:01.200
Those are your bosses.

00:27:01.580 --> 00:27:03.000
Uh, all very menacing.

00:27:03.220 --> 00:27:08.760
But they are, like, you know, significantly larger sprites, and no longer are you on a auto-scrolling thing.

00:27:08.760 --> 00:27:13.220
You're now, like, in their cave dungeon, uh, that you've entered.

00:27:13.220 --> 00:27:16.400
So there's some thematic building there, too, to, like, a bigger fight.

00:27:17.260 --> 00:27:19.080
What did we think of the boss fights, though?

00:27:19.260 --> 00:27:25.900
You know, a lot of times in shmups, it's, um, it's less about the boss itself, right?

00:27:26.020 --> 00:27:30.440
You just usually have to, like, shoot, uh, either a weak point or just the boss overall itself.

00:27:30.440 --> 00:27:36.180
But it's more about dealing with all the, uh, projectiles or enemies that also appear on stage.

00:27:36.340 --> 00:27:38.460
Did this game have, uh, a similar problem?

00:27:39.480 --> 00:27:42.460
The bosses were inconsequential in this game.

00:27:42.640 --> 00:27:49.580
Like, you've, you've removed, um, all of the mooks that would pester you and, like, sort of hit you otherwise.

00:27:50.320 --> 00:27:56.360
Um, you've removed the auto-scrolling, which, uh, thankfully gets rid of all the frustration of trying to jump over shit.

00:27:56.360 --> 00:28:01.360
Um, but also that removes all of the, uh, challenge.

00:28:01.660 --> 00:28:08.540
